pocket-motion-only: upstream ships this module to browsers and builds it on any host its contributors use, where a symlink in the crate is a broken checkout on Windows without core.symlinks and nothing hashes the module; here the module is the rasteriser every frame goes through, the package ships one copy of it, and its bytes should be the same wherever it was compiled.

0052 — the wasm crate reaches pocketjs-core through a path inside its own
workspace root, so the module's bytes do not depend on where the tree is.

Cargo gives rustc a `-C metadata` per crate, and rustc folds it into the
crate disambiguator every v0 symbol carries (`Cs1PSgNagyDwA_13pocketjs_wasm`).
For a path dependency the hash is of its path relative to the workspace
root when it is inside the root, and of its absolute path when it is not.
`engine/wasm` is a workspace of its own — upstream's `engine/Cargo.toml`
excludes it, for cargo-psp — so `path = "../core"` hashed the checkout's
location into pocketjs-core's disambiguator, and through it into the wasm
crate's. The disambiguators are in the name section, and they order the
module's functions, so the code and element sections moved too: two copies
of `engine/` built with the same rustc and every path remapped were the
same length and differed in 18,502 bytes, in the function, element, code and
name sections.

`engine/wasm/core` is a symlink to `../core`, and the dependency names it.
Cargo does not resolve the symlink, so pocketjs-core is inside the root,
becomes a member of the wasm crate's workspace, and is hashed as `core`;
as a member it is also handed to rustc by a relative path, so its panic
locations read `core/src/raster.rs` with no remap. `Cargo.lock` does not
record a path dependency's path and is unchanged. Built at two scratch
locations, the two modules were byte-identical; without this patch, not.

pocket-motion's `scripts/vendor.ts` remaps cargo's home for the registry
crates' panic locations. Neither changes a pixel: the ledger's digests are
the check.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

diff --git a/engine/wasm/Cargo.toml b/engine/wasm/Cargo.toml
index 08cb63e7..a34dde4f 100644
--- a/engine/wasm/Cargo.toml
+++ b/engine/wasm/Cargo.toml
@@ -16,7 +16,12 @@ edition = "2021"
 crate-type = ["cdylib"]
 
 [dependencies]
-pocketjs-core = { path = "../core" }
+# pocket-motion: `core` is a symlink to ../core. Cargo hashes a path
+# dependency into every symbol's crate disambiguator by its path relative to
+# the workspace root when it lies inside the root, and by its absolute path
+# when it does not, and the disambiguators order the module's functions. So
+# `../core` made the wasm's bytes depend on where the tree was checked out.
+pocketjs-core = { path = "core" }
 
 [profile.release]
 # pocket-motion: built for render throughput, not download size; the
diff --git a/engine/wasm/core b/engine/wasm/core
new file mode 120000
index 00000000..c73d9e17
--- /dev/null
+++ b/engine/wasm/core
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+../core
\ No newline at end of file
